  "id": "Compound::DB00482 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Celecoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, exhibits a complex interaction with cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, which are critical for drug metabolism. The visible evidence suggests that Celecoxib binds to CYP2D6 and CYP2C9, both of which are involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, a key step in the metabolism of various drugs. This binding leads to the activation of these enzymes, which in turn contribute to the metabolic pathway of arachidonic acid. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Celecoxib may influence CYP2C9 through its interaction with CYP2D6, which is a common mechanism in drug metabolism. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, supported by the shared participation of CYP2C9 in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of CYP2C9 in the metabolic activation of Celecoxib, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
